# Goal

Every terminal outcome of the Pi brew auto-updater (failed, skipped, contended, up-to-date, updated) reaches the user through `ui.notify`: a failure notifies on every startup at level `warning`; the manual command always reports its outcome; startup stays silent on non-failure outcomes unless something was updated.

This is correct only if:
- no terminal result is returned without passing the finish/shouldNotify pair;
- the tests would fail if a result were silently discarded again, with an oracle independent of the implementation;
- the recorded decisions in the issue document match what the code does;
- the new follow-up issue states a real, pre-existing gap (headless mode) without contradicting the settled policy.
